    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18431" root="زول" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوَّالٌ</span></b>  <i>Having much</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوْل</span>, i. e. <i>motion.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
Accord. to J, it occurs in an <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُرْجُوزَة</span>, cited by AA,
as meaning <i>That moves much in his gait, but
traverses a short space:</i> but the right word in
this case is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَوَّاك</span>, as is shown by the rhyme.
(IB, K.)

